Trailing Lambda Explanation
***************************

package com.androidtutorials.myapplication

fun main() {

    // Trailing Lambda Call
    demoLambda("Calling Lambda using Trailing") { a: Int, b: Int -> }

}

fun demoLambda(text: String, operation: (Int, Int) -> Unit) {
    println("Hello World")
}

/*
------------------------------------------------------------
TRAILING LAMBDA EXPLANATION
------------------------------------------------------------

If the last parameter of a function is a lambda,
Kotlin allows us to move that lambda outside the parentheses.

Example:

    demoLambda("Text") { a: Int, b: Int -> }

Here:
- "Text" is the first parameter (String).
- The lambda is the second and last parameter.
- Since it is the last parameter, we can write it
  outside the round brackets.

This improves readability and is commonly used in Kotlin.
The behavior remains exactly the same.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/
